            <ArticleTitle>Surface-gate-defined single-electron transistor in a MoS2 bilayer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125203</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1088/1361-6528/aa5ce0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the multi-scale modeling and design of a gate-defined single-electron transistor in a MoS2 bilayer. By combining density-functional theory and finite-element analysis, we design a surface gate structure to electrostatically define and tune a quantum dot and its associated tunnel barriers in the MoS2 bilayer. Our approach suggests new pathways for the creation of novel quantum electronic devices in two-dimensional materials.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
